\chapter{Project Definition \& Requirements}

\section{Project Mission \& High-Level Objectives}

The primary mission of SentinelShark is to empower security analysts with instant, automated visibility into network traffic risk without introducing operational complexity or high infrastructure overhead. Table~\ref{tab:objectives} itemizes the specific project objectives, their prioritized weight, and delivery status.

\begin{table}[htbp]
\centering
\caption{Project Objectives and Completion Status}
\label{tab:objectives}
\begin{tabularx}{\textwidth}{clXl}
\toprule
\textbf{ID} & \textbf{Priority} & \textbf{Objective Description} & \textbf{Status} \\
\midrule
O-01 & Critical & High-throughput packet capture via direct TShark JSON streaming & Complete \\
O-02 & Critical & Protocol dissection across OSI layers L2 through L7 into structured models & Complete \\
O-03 & Critical & Asynchronous threat intelligence query pipeline across 4 external APIs & Complete \\
O-04 & Critical & Robust fallback mechanism to simulated traffic (Mock Mode) when TShark absent & Complete \\
O-05 & High & Standard Wireshark-compatible binary PCAP/PCAPNG file import and export & Complete \\
O-06 & High & Real-time BPF capture filter sanitization and live table query filtering & Complete \\
O-07 & High & Visual threat triage via dynamic score calculation and row color coding & Complete \\
O-08 & High & In-memory TTL caching with completeness validation to conserve API quotas & Complete \\
O-09 & Medium & Full cross-platform compatibility on macOS 12+ and Windows 10/11 & Complete \\
O-10 & Low & Deliver a native C\# .NET 8 / WPF companion application for Windows & Complete \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabularx}
\end{table}

\section{System Scope}

\subsection{In Scope Capabilities}
\begin{itemize}[noitemsep]
  \item Live host network interface sniffing using line-buffered TShark JSON subprocess streams.
  \item Standard binary PCAP and PCAPNG file import with prompt-driven automated threat analysis.
  \item Native binary PCAP export using low-level \texttt{struct.pack} libpcap file formatting.
  \item Comprehensive protocol dissection: Ethernet, IPv4, IPv6, TCP, UDP, DNS, HTTP, HTTPS/TLS, SSH, ICMP, ARP, and QUIC.
  \item Automated threat enrichment querying AbuseIPDB, VirusTotal, IPinfo, and Shodan.
  \item Smart private IP filtering bypassing non-routable RFC 1918, loopback, and multicast addresses.
  \item In-memory thread-safe TTL caching with dynamic cache invalidation on credential update.
  \item Real-time BPF filter shortcut translator (\texttt{http}, \texttt{ssl}, \texttt{dns}, raw IP host wrapping).
  \item Figma-inspired dark cyber graphical user interface with live telemetry sparklines and metrics.
  \item Standalone unit test suite verifying caching, hashing, parsing, and filtering subsystems.
  \item Standalone Windows native .NET 8 / WPF companion application.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Out of Scope Boundaries}
\begin{itemize}[noitemsep]
  \item Active intrusion prevention (IPS) actions, such as automated firewall blocking or packet dropping.
  \item Persistent database storage (all capture telemetry and cached data remain strictly in-memory).
  \item Decryption of encrypted TLS application payloads without user-supplied private SSL keys.
  \item Outbound enterprise SIEM, Kafka, or Webhook streaming connectors.
  \item Wireless 802.11 monitor mode configuration or Bluetooth protocol parsing.
\end{itemize}

