%  CHAPTER 3: SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE & DATA ENGINEERING
% ============================================================
\chapter{System Architecture \& Data Engineering}

\section{Three-Tier Layered Architecture Pattern}

SentinelShark is architected around a strict three-tier modular pattern: the **UI Presentation Layer**, the **Core Processing Engine**, and the **Asynchronous Services Layer**. This separation ensures that high-velocity packet ingestion never starves the graphical user interface of execution time.

\begin{figure}[htbp]
\centering
\begin{tikzpicture}[node distance=0.45cm and 0.35cm]

  % UI Layer
  \node[ssbox, minimum width=2.5cm] (mw)  at (0.0, 6.8) {MainWindow};
  \node[ssbox, minimum width=2.5cm] (pt)  at (3.2, 6.8) {PacketTable};
  \node[ssbox, minimum width=2.5cm] (pd)  at (6.4, 6.8) {PacketDetail};
  \node[ssbox, minimum width=2.5cm] (hv)  at (9.6, 6.8) {HexView};
  \node[ssbox, minimum width=2.5cm] (sp)  at (12.8,6.8) {StatsPanel};
  \begin{scope}[on background layer]
    \node[draw=SSBlue!40, fill=SSCard, rounded corners=6pt, inner sep=6pt,
          fit=(mw)(pt)(pd)(hv)(sp)] (uilayer) {};
  \end{scope}
  \node[text=SSBlue, font=\scriptsize\bfseries] at (6.4, 7.4) {UI PRESENTATION LAYER --- PyQt6 Desktop Widgets};

  % Core Layer
  \node[ssmod] (cap)   at (1.2,  5.1) {capture.py};
  \node[ssmod] (par)   at (4.4,  5.1) {parser.py};
  \node[ssmod] (pcw)   at (7.6,  5.1) {pcapwriter.py};
  \node[ssmod] (imap)  at (10.8, 5.1) {interfacemapper.py};
