\section{Asynchronous Concurrency Model: qasync \& QThread}

Handling simultaneous 500+ packet/sec live capture while issuing concurrent HTTP REST requests requires a hybrid threading and asynchronous architecture:

\begin{enumerate}[noitemsep]
  \item \textbf{Dedicated Capture Thread (\texttt{QThread}):} The packet capture loop executes inside \texttt{LiveCaptureThread}, an isolated \texttt{QThread}. This prevents blocking the main GUI loop.
  \item \textbf{Asynchronous Event Loop (\texttt{qasync}):} Network lookups execute as \texttt{asyncio} coroutines managed by \texttt{qasync}, which embeds the Python asyncio event loop directly inside the PyQt6 Qt event loop.
  \item \textbf{Thread-Safe Signal Dispatching:} Inter-thread communication uses \texttt{pyqtSignal} objects (\texttt{packet\_received}, \texttt{packets\_batch\_received}, \texttt{threat\_resolved}, \texttt{queue\_status}), guaranteeing thread safety.
\end{enumerate}

\section{Technology Stack Specifications}

The technology stack powering SentinelShark was selected based on strict criteria of cross-platform stability, native rendering performance, and asynchronous non-blocking I/O efficiency. Rather than relying on web-based desktop wrappers (such as Electron) which introduce high memory footprints and garbage collection pauses, SentinelShark is built upon native compiled binaries and Python C-extensions.

\begin{itemize}[noitemsep]
  \item \textbf{PyQt6 GUI Toolkit:} Provides native desktop widgets with direct GPU acceleration, native OS styling, and high-performance paint events.
  \item \textbf{\texttt{qasync} Event Bridge:} Unifies the standard Python 3.10+ \texttt{asyncio} event loop with the Qt event loop, allowing non-blocking HTTP coroutines to update GUI elements without manual thread synchronization.
  \item \textbf{\texttt{httpx} Async Client:} Delivers fully asynchronous HTTP/1.1 and HTTP/2 transport pipelines with connection pooling, automatic keep-alive, and sub-millisecond connection reuse across threat intelligence providers.
  \item \textbf{\texttt{cachetools} Memory Cache:} Provides thread-safe, lock-optimized in-memory caching with Least-Recently-Used (LRU) eviction and time-to-live (TTL) expiration.
  \item \textbf{\texttt{psutil} Hardware Telemetry:} Facilitates real-time sampling of per-interface kernel byte counters to generate accurate bandwidth sparklines.
\end{itemize}

Table~\ref{tab:techstack} details each technology, the pinned dependency version, and its functional responsibility within the system.

