\section{Python Module Organization}

The Python codebase is partitioned into distinct subdirectories aligning with architectural boundaries:
\begin{itemize}[noitemsep]
  \item \textbf{Root \& Entry (\texttt{run.py}, \texttt{app/main.py}):} Bootstraps the application, configures the platform event loop policy (\texttt{WindowsSelectorEventLoopPolicy} on Windows), and starts the \texttt{qasync} loop.
  \item \textbf{Configuration Management (\texttt{app/config.py}):} Implements a thread-safe singleton managing \texttt{.env} secret isolation, \texttt{config.json} defaults, and automated discovery of the system TShark binary.
  \item \textbf{Core Packet Engine (\texttt{app/core/}):} Encapsulates packet capture (\texttt{capture.py}), layer dissection and hash calculation (\texttt{parser.py}), binary PCAP export (\texttt{pcapwriter.py}), TTL caching (\texttt{cache.py}), and cross-platform interface resolution (\texttt{interfacemapper.py}).
  \item \textbf{Services (\texttt{app/services/}):} Hosts the multi-provider async HTTP client (\texttt{threatintel.py}) and priority queue rate limiter (\texttt{queuemanager.py}).
  \item \textbf{UI Components (\texttt{app/ui/}):} Contains the main window frame (\texttt{mainwindow.py}), global dark cyber QSS stylesheet (\texttt{styles.py}), and modular UI components (\texttt{packettable.py}, \texttt{packetdetail.py}, \texttt{hexview.py}, \texttt{statspanel.py}, \texttt{sparkline.py}).
\end{itemize}

