\section{Unified Packet Data Model}

Every captured packet is parsed by \texttt{PacketDissector} into a unified dictionary structure. This model encapsulates all physical frame metadata, decoded protocol layers, raw byte arrays, pre-calculated payload hashes (MD5 and SHA256), and correlated threat intelligence. The schema fields and their data types are specified in Table~\ref{tab:packetmodel}.

\begin{table}[htbp]
\centering
\caption{Unified Packet Dictionary Structure}
\label{tab:packetmodel}
\begin{tabularx}{\textwidth}{>{\ttfamily\small}l >{\small}l X >{\small}l}
\toprule
\textbf{Field Name} & \textbf{Type} & \textbf{Description} & \textbf{Availability} \\
\midrule
no & int & Sequential packet index (1-based counter) & All Modes \\
time & str & Timestamp formatted as \texttt{HH:MM:SS.mmm} & All Modes \\
src & str & Source IPv4/IPv6 address or MAC & All Modes \\
dst & str & Destination IPv4/IPv6 address or MAC & All Modes \\
src\_port & str & Source transport layer port (e.g. 54321) & TCP / UDP \\
dst\_port & str & Destination transport layer port (e.g. 443) & TCP / UDP \\
protocol & str & Highest decoded OSI application/transport protocol & All Modes \\
length & int & Total frame length in bytes & All Modes \\
info & str & Summary dissection text (e.g. \texttt{GET /index.html}) & All Modes \\
raw\_bytes & bytes & Raw binary Ethernet payload bytes & Live / PCAP \\
hex\_dump & str & Pre-formatted offset, 16-hex, and ASCII string & All Modes \\
ascii\_str & str & Printable ASCII string representation of payload & All Modes \\
payload\_md5 & str & 32-character hexadecimal MD5 cryptographic hash & All Modes \\
payload\_sha256 & str & 64-character hexadecimal SHA256 hash & All Modes \\
layers\_tree & list & Hierarchical tree structure for OSI layer inspection & All Modes \\
threat\_score & int & Composite threat score (0 to 100) & Post-Lookup \\
threat\_data & dict & Aggregated dictionary of all 4 provider responses & Post-Lookup \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabularx}
\end{table}

