\section{Composite Threat Scoring \& Color Triage}

The composite threat score for each packet row is calculated dynamically:

\[
\text{Score} = \max\!\bigl(\text{AbuseIPDB Score},\; \text{VirusTotal Malicious Count} \times 20\bigr)
\]

If Shodan reports known CVE vulnerability identifiers and the preliminary score is below 50, the composite score is automatically elevated to \textbf{75} to highlight vulnerable infrastructure. The visual styling corresponding to each risk tier is outlined in Table~\ref{tab:colors}.

\begin{table}[htbp]
\centering
\caption{Threat Score Classification and Visual Color Coding}
\label{tab:colors}
\begin{tabular}{clllcl}
\toprule
