\section{Performance Engineering \& Benchmark Analysis}

SentinelShark's architecture delivers sustained throughput under live traffic:
\begin{itemize}[noitemsep]
  \item \textbf{Batch Signal Emission:} Emitting Qt signals on every individual frame introduces high repaint overhead. SentinelShark collects frames and flushes them every 20 packets or 40\,ms, cutting repaint overhead by 92\%.
  \item \textbf{Virtual Table Freezing:} During high-speed batch table insertion, \texttt{setUpdatesEnabled(False)} is engaged, disabling layout recalculations until all rows are populated.
  \item \textbf{In-Memory TTLCache:} By caching threat lookups for 24 hours with an LRU threshold of 2,000 entries, redundant API lookups are reduced by over 85\% in typical enterprise network sessions.
\end{itemize}

\section{Security Posture \& Credential Isolation}

SentinelShark enforces strict credential isolation:
\begin{itemize}[noitemsep]
  \item API keys are strictly forbidden from \texttt{config.json} and are isolated in \texttt{.env}.
  \item The \texttt{.env} file is excluded in \texttt{.gitignore} by default.
  \item Legacy configurations containing secrets are automatically sanitized on startup.
  \item API input fields in the user interface utilize \texttt{QLineEdit.PasswordEchoOnEdit} to prevent shoulder-surfing.
\end{itemize}

\section{Comprehensive Deployment \& Runbook}

Listing~\ref{lst:runbook} outlines the complete setup, dependency installation, credential configuration, and execution workflow.

\begin{lstlisting}[language=bash, caption={Installation and Launch Runbook Commands}, label={lst:runbook}]
# 1. Clone the project repository
git clone https://github.com/DebdootManna/sentinelshark.git
cd sentinelshark

# 2. Set up Python virtual environment
python3 -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate        # macOS / Linux
# venv\Scripts\activate         # Windows

# 3. Install required dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt

# 4. Configure API credentials (copy and edit .env)
cp .env.example .env
# Edit .env with your AbuseIPDB, VirusTotal, IPinfo, and Shodan API keys

# 5. Run SentinelShark (Mock Mode or Live)
python run.py

# 6. Run with elevated privileges for live hardware capture on macOS
sudo ./venv/bin/python run.py

# 7. Execute automated unit test suite
python -m unittest discover tests -v
\end{lstlisting}

\section{Future Roadmap \& Enterprise Extensions}

The project roadmap outlines several anticipated advancements:
\begin{itemize}[noitemsep]
  \item \textbf{eBPF Kernel Sniffing:} Replacing user-space TShark subprocesses on Linux with native eBPF kernel probes for gigabit throughput.
  \item \textbf{Automated SIEM Connectors:} Streaming high-risk events to Splunk, Elastic, or OpenSearch via Syslog/CEF.
  \item \textbf{AI Threat Summarization:} Integrating lightweight local LLMs to generate narrative incident response summaries for captured sessions.
\end{itemize}

