\chapter{.NET / WPF Companion Application}

\section{Architecture Overview}

\texttt{SentinelSharkDotNet} is a standalone, feature-complete Windows implementation of SentinelShark engineered in \textbf{C\# using WPF on .NET 8}. Published as a self-contained, single-file executable requiring no pre-installed .NET runtimes, it provides enterprise Windows deployments with direct integration into Windows networking APIs.

Table~\ref{tab:dotnet} specifies the build configuration, output binaries, and application manifest properties.

\begin{table}[htbp]
\centering
\caption{SentinelSharkDotNet Build Properties}
\label{tab:dotnet}
\begin{tabularx}{\textwidth}{lX}
\toprule
\textbf{Build Parameter} & \textbf{Specification / Value} \\
\midrule
Target Framework & \texttt{net8.0-windows} \\
Output Binary Type & Windows GUI Application (\texttt{WinExe}) \\
Assembly Name & \texttt{SentinelShark.exe} \\
Deployment Packaging & Self-contained, single-file executable (\texttt{PublishSingleFile=true}) \\
Runtime Identifier & Windows 64-bit (\texttt{win-x64}) \\
Assembly Compression & High compression enabled for minimal binary footprint \\
Security Manifest & Automated UAC elevation request for raw socket/Npcap access \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabularx}
\end{table}

\section{C\# Module Reference \& Component Mapping}

The C\# codebase mirrors the Python application's modular separation across Core, Models, Services, and UI layers. Table~\ref{tab:dotnetmodules} provides the file-level responsibility breakdown.

\begin{table}[htbp]
\centering
\caption{.NET Application Module Organization}
\label{tab:dotnetmodules}
\begin{tabularx}{\textwidth}{llX}
\toprule
\textbf{Source File} & \textbf{Layer} & \textbf{Component Responsibility} \\
\midrule
\texttt{Core/AppConfig.cs} & Config & Singleton parser for \texttt{.env} and JSON settings \\
\texttt{Core/CaptureEngine.cs} & Core & TShark subprocess capture and stdout stream processing \\
\texttt{Core/PacketParser.cs} & Core & Layer tree parser, byte dissection, and MD5/SHA256 hashing \\
\texttt{Core/InterfaceMapper.cs} & Core & Windows Registry query mapping NPF GUIDs to friendly NIC names \\
\texttt{Core/PcapWriter.cs} & Core & Native binary libpcap exporter \\
\texttt{Core/ThreatCache.cs} & Core & In-memory thread-safe TTL cache with completeness checks \\
\texttt{Models/PacketInfo.cs} & Model & Unified packet data structure \\
\texttt{Models/ThreatData.cs} & Model & Multi-feed threat intelligence data container \\
\texttt{Services/ThreatIntelClient.cs} & Service & Asynchronous HttpClient querying AbuseIPDB, VT, IPinfo, Shodan \\
\texttt{Services/ThreatQueueManager.cs} & Service & Channel-based rate limiter with exponential backoff \\
\texttt{UI/MainWindow.xaml(.cs)} & UI & WPF window with splitters mirroring PyQt6 layout \\
\texttt{UI/Controls/SparklineControl.cs} & UI & Custom WPF \texttt{FrameworkElement} with hardware-accelerated wave \\
\texttt{Themes/DarkTheme.xaml} & UI & 42KB comprehensive WPF dark cyber resource dictionary \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabularx}
\end{table}

